Licensing rationale
------------------------------------------------------------------------

go-seccure is a clean-room reimplementation: we read the references but do
not copy code from them. The Go library is therefore independently
copyrightable, and Invenity Labs licenses it under LGPL-3.0 to match the
byte-level parity target (py-seccure) and to permit dynamic linking from
proprietary downstream consumers.

The vendored reference sources under reference/c/ and reference/py/ retain
their upstream licenses (GPL-2.0-or-later and LGPL-3.0-or-later respectively),
unmodified. See each subdirectory's LICENSE.upstream for the canonical text.
They are present for offline cross-checking against the authoritative wire
format; they are NOT compiled or imported by any code in this repository.
